{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476294647,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MzI4Njk2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/992#issuecomment-253286960"},"message":"yeah -- I also wanted something like that in `ls` output.  Want to see what has changed from the committed state. Or ideally even from some remote sibling I would specify (e.g. `datalad-public` corresponding to datasets.datalad.org).\nPartially could be mitigated I guess whenever someone creates 'foreach' command (#749). Also as a local workaround for quickly checking what has happened I came up with ['lgl' alias for my gitcofig](http://git.onerussian.com/?p=etc/base.git;a=blob;f=.gitconfig;h=998a2661aa66a9f5451f6befd592280083e72059;hb=HEAD#l24)\n\n``` shell\nhopa:~/datalad/openfmri/ds000001\n$\u003e git lgl            \n7ec9ffdb  [DATALAD] aggregated meta data                         2.0.1  1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)\nbc151f5d  [DATALAD] record generated dataset ID     2.0.0+4-4-gbc151f5  1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)\nb279f77a  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'         2.0.0+4-3-gb279f77  52 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)\ncc6a09ac  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                    2.0.0+4  2 files changed, 2 deletions(-)\n0b449de8  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                    2.0.0+3  2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n16f75741  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                    2.0.0+2  2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n452a3aee  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                    2.0.0+1  2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n05e9fb9c  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                      2.0.0  1442 files changed, 148 insertions(+), 1337 deletions(-)\n14a8dd42  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                    1.1.0+1  2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n68bb4ac1  Adjusted crawler configuration: crawl:p     1.1.0-1-g68bb4ac  1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n3ad92404  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                      1.1.0  115 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 113 deletions(-)\n2ed6cc0a  Merge branch 'incoming-processed'                      1.0.0  1344 files changed, 1423 insertions(+)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1489077154,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4NTQwMzc3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/992#issuecomment-285403776"},"message":"Now that @bpoldrack spend much time on testing the behavior of `status` under all conditions, maybe it is time to pour this knowledge into a simple `status` command. If we had such, we might make use of it for datalad internals also, rather then exploring `git status` and `git annex status` edge cases every single time.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1489080052,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4NTQxODM5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/992#issuecomment-285418396"},"message":"I could provide a command exposing `Repo.status`, but depends on what we expect this to do.\nNote, that `git annex status` itself provides less information about submodules than `git status` does. They are just reported 'modified' no matter whether the 'modification' is untracked content or an actual modification. And it does not distinguish between staged and unstaged changes (for a reason).\nTherefore I'm not sure about the value of a `datalad status` in addition to `datalad ls`.\nIt could be a simple `git annex status` (one that does not fail in submodules without working trees) for a quick overview of a given (CWD?) dataset. Question is: Is this what you imagine?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1489080560,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ2